{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the neuro-oncology team. You’re here today for your 19th cycle of high-dose methotrexate. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m okay. A little tired lately, but otherwise fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you started rituximab two weeks ago. That’s part of the new alternating regimen. Any side effects from that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not really. Just felt a bit flushed during the infusion, but it passed quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common and usually mild. We’ll monitor you closely today. We’ll give the methotrexate around noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Do I need any special prep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll start IV fluids to protect your kidneys and give sodium bicarbonate to keep your urine alkaline. That helps clear the methotrexate faster."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the leucovorin? When does that start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start leucovorin 24 hours after the methotrexate. It helps protect your healthy cells from the chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll stay here until the level drops low enough?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2176-05-31 10:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll check your methotrexate level daily. Once it’s below 0.2, and you’re stable, you can go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2176-05-31 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The methotrexate infusion is complete. You did well. Any nausea or headache so far?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2176-05-31 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just a little queasy, nothing bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2176-05-31 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you some lorazepam or compazine if it gets worse. We’re avoiding Zofran because it gave you headaches before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2176-05-31 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. That’s better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2176-06-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs look stable. Liver enzymes are slightly up, but that’s expected. Your creatinine is low at 0.5, so kidneys are doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2176-06-01 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What about the methotrexate level?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2176-06-01 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s at 0.48. Still a bit high, so we’ll keep going with fluids and bicarbonate. Leucovorin started last night as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2176-06-01 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my aspirin—I usually take that daily. Should I restart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2176-06-01 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We held it to help the methotrexate clear faster. You’re getting heparin shots for clot prevention. We’ll restart aspirin when you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2176-06-01 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Great news—your methotrexate level is now 0.14. That’s low enough for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief! So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, once we go over your discharge instructions. You’ll need to take leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate every six hours for three more days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same doses as in the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—40 mg leucovorin and 1300 mg sodium bicarbonate every six hours. It’s important to finish all the doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my regular meds—can I restart everything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. All your usual medications—citalopram, gabapentin, asthma inhalers, and aspirin—should be restarted today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My foot pain has been acting up. Is that still something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s still chronic and not fully explained, but we don’t think it’s related to the lymphoma. Keep using gabapentin and oxycodone as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I see someone about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, follow up with your primary doctor. Maybe a neurology or pain specialist can help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your liver enzymes are a bit higher than baseline—31 for ALT, 37 for AST—but that’s mild and expected with methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No need for concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at this level. We’ll watch it next cycle. Your hemoglobin is stable at 10.7, so no anemia issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my mood’s been okay. Citalopram is helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad to hear that. You’ve been through a lot, but you’re managing well. Keep taking it daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And the next chemo is in a month?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, same plan—alternating methotrexate and rituximab. The oncology clinic will call to schedule it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I appreciate all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2176-06-02 06:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did great this cycle. Take care, and call if you have any problems."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2176-06-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick final check before discharge. You’re alert, vitals are stable, and labs are good. Ready to go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2176-06-03 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, definitely. I’m feeling well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2176-06-03 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Remember—leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate every six hours for three days. And follow up with your team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2176-06-03 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve got it written down. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2176-06-03 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you next month."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2176-05-31 10:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2176-06-03 09:50:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old woman with primary central nervous system lymphoma, ulcerative colitis, asthma, and a history of DVT/PE was admitted for her 19th cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. She tolerated the treatment well with only mild nausea, which was managed with lorazepam and prochlorperazine. Methotrexate levels were monitored daily, declining to 0.14 uM by discharge, allowing safe transition home. Leucovorin rescue and sodium bicarbonate were administered as scheduled to support methotrexate clearance. Aspirin was held during admission and restarted at discharge, with heparin used for DVT prophylaxis. Liver enzymes showed mild, expected elevation, and her hemoglobin remained stable. She reported ongoing chronic right foot pain, managed with gabapentin and PRN oxycodone, and denied depressive symptoms, remaining on citalopram. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to complete three days of leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate and to continue alternating methotrexate and rituximab therapy.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Primary central nervous system lymphoma, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Nonspecific elevation of levels of transaminase or lactic acid dehydrogenase [LDH]",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism",
      "Antineoplastic chemotherapy induced anemia",
      "Antineoplastic and immunosuppressive drugs causing adverse effects in therapeutic use",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
